---
// roadmap.astro - Official AFWE ReBorn Phased Roadmap
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Roadmap · AFWE ReBorn Trajectory"
  description="The architectural trajectory of AFWE: from deterministic AST tripwires to multi-agent working tree leases and autonomous drift healing."
  activeNav="roadmap"
>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-20 space-y-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="space-y-4 border-b border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 pb-8">
      <div class="text-[11px] font-mono font-bold tracking-[0.2em] text-survey-600 dark:text-survey-light uppercase">
        ARCHITECTURAL TRAJECTORY
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold font-bold text-graphite dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        AFWE ReBorn Roadmap
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-graphite/80 dark:text-stone-300 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        We build AFWE in grounded, testable phases. Every milestone represents a working deterministic capability in Rust, verified against real codebases.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Phased Roadmap Stack -->
    <div class="space-y-12">
      <!-- Phase 0: Shipped -->
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-400/80 dark:border-obsidian-700 bg-white/70 dark:bg-obsidian-900 p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-stone-200 dark:border-obsidian-800 pb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="size-3 rounded-full bg-afwe-commit"></span>
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold font-bold text-graphite dark:text-white">Phase 0: Kernel & Tripwires</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-500/30">
            Shipped & Verified
          </span>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-graphite/80 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          The foundation of double-entry bookkeeping: deterministic AST scene graphing and tamper-proof architectural tripwires.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Tree-Sitter Multi-Language Scene Graph</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              Native AST parsing for Rust, TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and Go. Symbols resolve to persistent identities without relying on brittle line numbers.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">BLAKE3 Manifest & Pre-Commit Hook</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              Cryptographic manifest prevents agents from tampering with guardrail files. Chained git hook runs verification before commits hit the repo.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Phase 1: Shipped / Live -->
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-400/80 dark:border-obsidian-700 bg-white/70 dark:bg-obsidian-900 p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-stone-200 dark:border-obsidian-800 pb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="size-3 rounded-full bg-afwe-commit"></span>
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold font-bold text-graphite dark:text-white">Phase 1: Semantic Intent & Probing Guides</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-500/30">
            Shipped & Live
          </span>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-graphite/80 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          Eliminating raw LLM confidence floats with an additive deterministic calibration rubric and anti-echo-chamber hold-out probes.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Additive Calibration Rubric</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              Calculates confidence from verifiable evidence (floor 0.50, +0.25 AST claims, +0.10 sibling consistency) and immediately caps at 0.40 on contradiction.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Hold-Out Probing Guides</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              Rules with confidence between 0.85 and 0.90 advise the agent. To become blocking checks, they must pass a hold-out test where the rule was deliberately withheld.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Phase 2: Shipped / Live -->
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-400/80 dark:border-obsidian-700 bg-white/70 dark:bg-obsidian-900 p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-stone-200 dark:border-obsidian-800 pb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="size-3 rounded-full bg-afwe-commit"></span>
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold font-bold text-graphite dark:text-white">Phase 2: 4D Time Dial & Ghost Recovery</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-500/30">
            Shipped & Live
          </span>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-graphite/80 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          Treating time as an interactive dial rather than a flat commit log, enabling automated detection and 3-way merge recovery of dropped features.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Ghost Node Detection</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              Surfaces features or components that an agent inadvertently removed during large refactors, highlighting collateral loss before merge.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">One-Command Feature Restoration</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              <code class="text-survey-600 dark:text-survey-light">afwe timeline restore &lt;feature&gt;</code> executes a true 3-way AST merge and stages the fix cleanly in a new turn.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Phase 3: Active / In Progress -->
      <section class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-survey-500/60 dark:border-survey-500/40 bg-white/80 dark:bg-obsidian-900 p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-stone-200 dark:border-obsidian-800 pb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="size-3 rounded-full bg-survey-500 animate-pulse"></span>
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold font-bold text-graphite dark:text-white">Phase 3: Multi-Agent Leases & Studio Canvas</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-survey-500/15 text-survey-700 dark:text-survey-light border border-survey-500/30">
            Active / In Progress
          </span>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-graphite/80 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          Enabling multiple concurrent agents to work in isolated tree leases without stepping on each other's boundaries, backed by the interactive Studio.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Concurrent Tree Leases</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              <code class="text-survey-600 dark:text-survey-light">afwe lease acquire</code> partitions the AST scene graph so Claude Code and Cursor can work simultaneously.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Adaptive Studio Canvas</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              Dual-mode visual cockpit: Radial Sunburst for macro subsystem zoning + Topology Map for micro-dependencies and active constraint violations.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">57 MCP Server Tools</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              First-class Model Context Protocol integration exposing turn lifecycle, pin queries, and constraint verification directly to agents.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Phase 4: Planned / Next -->
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-white/40 dark:bg-obsidian-900/60 p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 opacity-90">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-stone-200 dark:border-obsidian-800 pb-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="size-3 rounded-full bg-stone-400 dark:bg-stone-600"></span>
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold font-bold text-graphite dark:text-white">Phase 4: Autonomous Drift Healing & Global Memory</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-stone-300/40 text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 border border-stone-400/40">
            Planned / Next
          </span>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-graphite/80 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          Proactive reconciliation of manual human commits and cross-repository architectural pattern learning.
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Autonomous Drift Reconciliation</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              Detects manual edits made outside turn protocols and synthesizes backward-compatible turn receipts to maintain invariant continuity.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-obsidian-800 bg-paper/50 dark:bg-obsidian-850">
            <div class="font-bold text-graphite dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">Reusable Boundary Packs</div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-graphite/70 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans">
              Export and import verified constraint packages (Clean Architecture, Hexagonal, Microservice Boundaries) across enterprise workspace fleets.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>

